From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:39:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Let the requests queued behind a gone global's
 upgrade go on

When a global goes away while one of its open requests runs its upgrade
transaction, the factory's teardown sends AbortPendingUpgrades, and the
manager takes the request out of the connection queue and reverts the
upgrade. It didn't advance the queue, though: the open and delete
requests of other globals queued behind the removed one waited forever.
abort_pending_upgrades now advances the queue when the request it
removed was the one running, as abort_pending_upgrade (one request, from
an aborted upgrade transaction) already did.

Found with a fork WPT test that removes an iframe while its upgrade
populates an index; the P3.1 binary hangs the same way without any
createIndex, so the bug predates the population.

Validation: New integration test test_indexeddb_aborted_pending_upgrade_lets_the_next_open_run (an open request queued behind one whose global sends AbortPendingUpgrades during its upgrade gets its upgrade): passes on SQLite, fails after 5 s without the fix; `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` 134 passed, 1 skipped. New fork test tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/IndexedDB/removed-iframe-during-upgrade.html (an iframe removed during its upgrade, without and with a createIndex that populates 5,000 records; the parent then opens and writes): 2 of 2 on SM, QuickJS and the DAYU200, TIMEOUT with the P3.1 binary already in the first subtest; removed-iframe-aborts-its-transactions.html still passes. Host WPT tests/wpt/tests/IndexedDB at this commit: SpiderMonkey 3,392, QuickJS 3,389 of 4,511, the same as the previous commit's results reported there; /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 172 of 172 on SM, QuickJS, SM --multiprocess and the DAYU200; DAYU200 WPT IndexedDB/ 3,381 (QuickJS + RDB). These counts predate the P3 review fixes folded into the P3.1 and P3.2 commits, which add a backend test and fork subtests.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; found the hang with a new WPT test, fixed the queue advance, wrote the integration and WPT tests, ran them)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/storage/indexeddb/mod.rs           | 16 +++--
 components/storage/tests/indexeddb.rs         | 44 +++++++++++-
 tests/wpt/mozilla/meta/MANIFEST.json          | 13 ++++
 .../removed-iframe-during-upgrade.html        | 69 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../IndexedDB/resources/upgrade-frame.html    | 14 ++++
 5 files changed, 151 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/IndexedDB/removed-iframe-during-upgrade.html
